2:T7af,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to fit a kitchen in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a small, straightforward kitchen may typically cost around £4,000, while a large or higher-spec project may cost £25,000 or more. The final cost depends on units, worktops, layout, labour and building services. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is usually included in a kitchen fitting price?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It may include cabinet assembly and installation, worktops, plinths, doors, handles and some appliance connections. Removal, waste disposal, plumbing, electrical work, tiling, flooring and decorating may be separate, so check the written quotation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to keep the same kitchen layout?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Retaining sink, dishwasher, cooker and appliance positions can reduce plumbing, electrical and preparation work. However, the existing services still need to be checked and any saving depends on the condition of the room."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I reduce my kitchen fitting cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keep the layout straightforward, avoid unnecessary service moves, compare complete specifications rather than headline prices, and confirm what labour and finishing work are included. Choosing practical materials can also reduce the total without changing the layout."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a kitchen cost calculator replace a quotation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A calculator is useful for early budgeting, but it cannot assess access, uneven floors, hidden damage, existing wiring or the exact products selected. A site assessment and itemised quotation can provide a more reliable figure."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitting-cost-calculator-uk","d"]
