,"path","1cmpym",{"d":"M8 2v4"}],["$","path","4m81vk",{"d":"M16 2v4"}],["$","rect","1hopcy",{"width":"18","height":"18","x":"3","y":"4","rx":"2"}],["$","path","8toen8",{"d":"M3 10h18"}],"$undefined"]}],"30 July 2026",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/25","children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"BMB Renovation"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-14 sm:py-20 flex-grow bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Planning a new kitchen is easier when you can see how each decision may affect the budget. This kitchen fitting cost calculator UK guide gives you a practical early estimate based on kitchen size, layout, materials, labour and optional plumbing or electrical work. It is intended for early planning rather than a fixed quotation: prices vary with the condition of the room, product specification, access and the amount of preparation required."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Kitchen fitting cost calculator UK"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["To use the calculator, choose the options that most closely match your project, then add the relevant figures. Start with the number of kitchen units rather than the overall floor area, as fitting costs are often linked to the number and type of cabinets, appliances and worktop sections. The figures below are rough UK planning allowances only. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Kitchen size: small, up to around 8 units; medium, around 9 to 14 units; or large, around 15 to 20 units."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Layout: a straightforward single-wall or galley layout; an L-shaped layout; or a U-shaped layout with more corners and cuts."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Materials: entry-level or flat-pack cabinets; mid-range cabinets and laminate worktops; or higher-spec cabinets with premium worktops."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Labour: cabinet installation, worktop fitting, appliance installation, plinths, handles, adjustments and making good."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Plumbing: retain the existing sink, dishwasher and washing machine positions, or allow for moving one or more water and waste connections."]}]]}],["$","li","5",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Electrical work: retain the existing points, or allow for additional sockets, lighting, appliance supplies or circuit alterations."]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Thinking about your own project?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation covers Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead and beyond — all trades in-house. Call +44 7775 758 717 or send us a message."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get a Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Illustrative cost bands"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["As a rough guide, a small, straightforward kitchen may typically cost around £4,000 to £8,000 for cabinets, basic worktops and fitting, before major plumbing, electrical changes, flooring or decoration."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["As a rough guide, a medium kitchen may typically cost around £7,000 to £14,000 for a mid-range installation with standard worktops and typical fitting requirements."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["As a rough guide, a large or higher-spec kitchen may typically cost around £12,000 to £25,000 or more where there are more units, an island, premium worktops, bespoke details or extensive preparation."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["As a rough guide, modest additional plumbing changes may typically cost around £300 to £1,500, depending on how far services must move and whether floors or walls need opening."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["As a rough guide, additional electrical work may typically cost around £400 to £2,000 for extra sockets, lighting and appliance connections; more complex work may cost more."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"How to calculate your estimated kitchen fitting cost"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A simple calculation is: materials and cabinets + worktops + labour + plumbing changes + electrical changes + preparation and finishing. For example only, a medium kitchen might allow £6,000 for cabinets and worktops, £3,000 for fitting, £600 for plumbing and £800 for electrical work. This would give an early estimate of £10,400 before flooring, plastering, decorating or unexpected repairs. These are rough planning figures, not a standard price: every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"What kitchen fitting labour normally includes"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Kitchen fitting labour can cover assembling and securing cabinets, levelling units, fitting doors and drawers, installing plinths, fitting handles, cutting and joining worktops, and connecting appliances where appropriate. It may also include removing the old kitchen, protecting nearby areas and making minor adjustments. Ask for a written breakdown so you can see whether waste removal, appliance connections, silicone finishing and final cleaning are included."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Cabinet installation: more units, tall housings, corner mechanisms and an island can increase the time required."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Worktops: laminate can often be cut on site, while solid timber, stone or compact surfaces may require specialist templating and fabrication."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Layout changes: moving a sink, dishwasher, cooker or radiator can add preparation, service alterations and reinstatement work."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Room condition: uneven floors, damaged plaster, poor walls, old wiring and hidden leaks can affect the final cost."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Finishing work: tiling, flooring, painting, splashbacks and decorating may be separate from the basic cabinet fitting allowance."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"How kitchen size and layout affect the estimate"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A small kitchen is not always the cheapest to fit. Limited access, awkward corners and several appliances packed into a compact space can make installation slower. A galley kitchen may have fewer units but can still require careful levelling and detailed worktop joins. L-shaped and U-shaped kitchens often involve more corner units, return panels and worktop cuts. An island adds cabinets, panels, worktop, flooring considerations and sometimes new electrical supplies, so it should be treated as a separate part of the estimate."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Plumbing and electrical costs to include"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Keeping the sink and appliances close to their existing positions can help control costs, although the condition of the current connections still needs checking. Moving services may involve lifting flooring, opening walls or altering pipework and cables. Electrical requirements depend on the appliances and the existing installation. Your estimate should identify whether it includes socket changes, lighting, extractor connections, cooker supplies and any inspection or certification needed for the work. Do not rely on a calculator alone where the existing installation has not been inspected."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Getting a more accurate kitchen installation estimate"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Before comparing quotes, prepare a basic plan showing room dimensions, doors, windows, radiators, existing service points and appliance positions. List which items you are supplying and which the installer is supplying. Also state whether the project includes removal and disposal, plaster repairs, tiling, flooring, decorating and appliance connections. This makes quotations easier to compare and can reduce the risk of important work being left out."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["For homeowners in and around Watford, a site visit can help replace a broad calculator range with a project-specific figure. BMB Renovation provides kitchen fitting and renovation, with plumbing, tiling, electrical and cabinet installation handled in-house. You can learn more about ",["$","$L4","0",{"href":"/kitchen-renovation-watford","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"kitchen renovation in Watford"}],", review the wider ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/kitchen-fitting-watford","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"kitchen fitting service"}],", or request a ",["$","$L4","2",{"href":"/contact","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"free, no-obligation quote"}],"."]}],["$","aside",nu